 early out-neighbours are {29, 332, 1327, 1692} (step_09) and 908's only later in-neighbours are {227, 551, 641} (step_08); the in-neighbours of those three relays are {209,1329,1569,1909}, {153,723,1037,1193} and {304,1210} (step_10, step_11, step_12), none of which is reachable from 60's early out-set, and the one high-degree relay candidate 153 is fed by 88 nodes none of which is 60 or one of 60's out-neighbours (step_13), confirming 153 is a generic hub rather than a cascade carrier. A 1-hop check around 908 in the late window shows only a single reciprocal contact with 1350 (step_14), i.e. 908 is essentially inert during the period when 60 is most active. No chain of interactions with successive gaps of at most 600 time units can therefore link 60 to 908.", "confidence": 0.87, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "{\"task_id\":\"t_64416af4\",\"decision\":\"absent\",\"mechanism\":\"cascade\",\"entities\":[60,908],\"window\":[30939,69338],\"narrative\":\"Node 60 has 19 events and node 908 has 23 events in the window (step_02), so both are active enough that a cascade was in principle observable \u2014 volume is not the limiting factor. However, 60's out-neighbourhood (18 nodes: 29, 155, 332, 487, 617, 703, 751, 768, 974, 1055, 1070, 1327, 1443, 1531, 1692, 1694, 1762, 1830; step_04) is disjoint from 908's in-neighbourhood (18 nodes: 18, 173, 227, 534, 551, 575, 632, 641, 683, 723, 741, 904, 952, 1426, 1517, 1555,